group: Td
formula: Ni(CO)4
construction: Fragment orbitals (extended Hückel)
headline: 
note: Model from extended Hückel (qualitative) · model energies in eV · calculation in Hartree · labels in T<sub>d</sub>\n1 empty model orbital lies more than 30 eV above the HOMO; it is drawn at the top of the axis (marked ↑) with the model energy beside it.\n4 empty model orbitals lie more than 30 eV above the HOMO and sit almost entirely on one fragment; not drawn.\n1 model level has no close calculated counterpart (overlap below 0.80); read its calculated energy with care.
about: **The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (Ni and (CO)4). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments, then paired per symmetry label and degeneracy, so each antibonding level has its bonding partner; a level without a partner is non-bonding. Colours mark the pairs.\n\n**The calculation** is the narrow column on the right. For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, its energy in Hartree and the overlap value (1 is identical). Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\n**Total electrons: 50** (Ni 10, (CO)4 40).\n\nThe grey bars are model levels that sit almost entirely on the (CO)4 and take no part in the interaction; they are counted, not drawn.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in Td; the code reported none.
verdict: differs Model and calculation disagree on the order of 1 of 28 pairs of the 8 valence levels (overlap 0.68–0.99): 12T2* / 10A1*.
